@page "/release-notes"

@* The Release Notes (ADR-0190), a reference page: every version published to nuget.org up to the one the
   site was published for, newest first, one anchor each, read at build time from docs/releases/. The site
   follows the newest version tagged, a prerelease included (ADR-0205, 2026-11-03), so only a patch's notes
   to an older line, tagged below a later version, are on its GitHub release alone. A site not published
   from a tag also shows what is unreleased, from the Change Notes. Its sections are the versions, which
   the rail lists. *@
<DocsPage Title="Release notes"
          Lead="Every version published to nuget.org up to the one this site describes, newest first. A version's packages ship together, at one version, from one tag. This site describes the newest version published, a prerelease included; a patch to an older line, published after a later version, has its notes on its GitHub release.">
    <ReleaseNotesView />
</DocsPage>
